. QUICK START\n36: \n37: **Step 1: Confirm the owner.**\n38: \n39: Start with `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md` for runtime routing and workflow boundaries.\n40: \n41: **Step 2: Inspect the local code.**\n42: \n43: ```bash\n44: rg --files .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy\n45: ```\n46: \n47: Expected result: the command lists the source files summarized below.\n48: \n49: **Step 3: Verify changes.**\n50: \n51: Run individual scripts from the repository root with the documented arguments.\n52: \n53: ---\n54: \n55: ## 3. FEATURES\n56: \n57: | Feature | What It Does |\n58: |---|---|\n59: | Folder boundary | Documents direct code files under `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy`. |\n60: | sk-code alignment | Points reviewers at OpenCode naming, header, error-handling and type-discipline checks. |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md, lines 1-60\n1: ---\n2: title: \"system skill advisor runtime scripts routing accuracy: Code README\"\n3: description: \"Code-facing README for .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"system-skill-advisor runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy\"\n6:   - \"code README\"\n7: ---\n8: \n9: # system skill advisor runtime scripts routing accuracy\n10: \n11: Operator and maintenance scripts for this skill.\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n16: \n17: ### Purpose\n18: \n19: This README documents the code-bearing folder `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy` so operators can understand its role without opening every source file first. It follows the sk-doc skill README structure while staying focused on code navigation.\n20: \n21: ### Usage\n